items.statement:
At an ordinary point x ∈ (𝔈_{p,2})^{≥1}, exactly one of the following holds for p_1^*H → p_2^*H:
1. both are multiplicative and the map is an isomorphism; then p_2^*I^{−1} → p_1^*I^{−1} is an isomorphism at x;
2. both are étale and the map is an isomorphism; then p_2^*I^{−1} → p_1^*I^{−1} is an isomorphism at x;
3. p_1^*H is étale, p_2^*H is multiplicative and the map is zero at x; then p_2^*I^{−1} → p_1^*I^{−1} factors through p·p_1^*I^{−1} over the local ring at x.
